      "side": 1,
      "message": "This magic number forces the reader to look up the bit definition.\n\nIf you use the bitfield names, it\u0027s a lot clearer of the intent.\n```\n.bits.command_completed \u003d 1,\n.bits.external_supply_change \u003d 1,\n.bits.power_operation_mode_change \u003d 1,\n/* ... */\n```\n\nWhen this gets moved to the devicetree, it will be much easier for a reviewer to confirm correctness.  You can then revert back to using the raw_value.\n\n```\n/* DT policy */\n.notifications \u003d \u003c(COMMAND_COMPLETE\n    | EXTERNAL_SUPPLY_CHANGE\n    | POWER_OPERATION_MODE_CHANGE\n    | /* ... */)\u003e;\n    \n/* Driver code */\n.bits.raw_value \u003d DT_PROP(notifications),\n```",
